From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OBS AirPlay Sender contributors
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Use core-only AAC-ELD when MPS is disabled

libxaac currently treats every AAC-ELD configuration without MPS as
ELD-SBR. That consumes 960 PCM samples at 44.1 kHz to emit a 480-core
access unit, which is incompatible with the AirPlay/Douyin requirement
for one 480-sample PCM frame per raw access unit.

Keep the existing ELD-SBR behavior for ELDv2/MPS, but let the core AAC-ELD
encoder handle the no-MPS case. The OBS AirPlay helper verifies the
resulting 1920-byte input frame and 44100 Hz time base at startup.
---
 encoder/ixheaace_api.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/encoder/ixheaace_api.c b/encoder/ixheaace_api.c
index 943d6f9..a45baa6 100644
--- a/encoder/ixheaace_api.c
+++ b/encoder/ixheaace_api.c
@@ -906,7 +906,7 @@ static IA_ERRORCODE ixheaace_set_config_params(ixheaace_api_struct *pstr_api_str
       }
     }
-    if ((AOT_SBR == pstr_input_config->aot) || (AOT_PS == pstr_input_config->aot) ||
-        (AOT_AAC_ELD == pstr_input_config->aot)) {
+    if ((AOT_SBR == pstr_input_config->aot) || (AOT_PS == pstr_input_config->aot) ||
+        ((AOT_AAC_ELD == pstr_input_config->aot) && (pstr_input_config->i_use_mps == 1))) {
       pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].aac_classic = 0;
     }
     if (pstr_api_struct->config[ele_idx].sample_rate < 32000) {
